=== [Judge Iter 0019] 2026-09-16 13:15:15 | Rubric Focus: Feature Engineering ===
Judge Question: "Explain the mathematics of Tree-Path Decomposition (Saabas 2014) in deriving unit-level stress contributions."
Context: Island=Tioman, Tab=evidence
Model Defense (3.90s) | Title: Methodology: Tree-Path Decomposition (Saabas 2014) | Pose: answer | Links: 1
  [CONCEPT]:
    The stress factor contribution is derived by tracing the decision path of a specific monitoring unit through every tree in the Gradient Boosting Regressor ensemble. This method attributes the predicted change in live coral cover (LCC) to specific input features by calculating the difference in node values along the path.
  [MATHEMATICAL ATTRIBUTION]:
    1. Path Traversal: For a given unit, the model identifies the unique path taken through each tree based on feature values (e.g., substrate, fish counts, pollution indicators).
2. Contribution Calculation: The contribution of a feature is the sum of the differences in predicted values at each node split where that feature was the decision variable.
3. Aggregation: The final stress factor contribution is the average of these path-based differences across all trees in the ensemble, providing a granular view of what drives the predicted decline or growth.
  [MODEL CONTEXT]:
    This approach allows ReefSafe to isolate the impact of specific environmental and anthropogenic variables from the baseline, ensuring that the 5.862 pp/yr MAE is transparently linked to measurable ecological indicators rather than external climate proxies like NOAA DHW.
  [CITATIONS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports

