=== [Judge Iter 0084] 2026-09-16 13:21:54 | Rubric Focus: Validation Rigor ===
Judge Question: "How is the 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution of [-16.25, +13.66 pp/yr] computed?"
Context: Island=Perhentian, Tab=diagnostics
Model Defense (2.41s) | Title: Model Uncertainty Analysis: Residual Distribution | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [METHODOLOGY]:
    The 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution is derived from a walk-forward validation process using the Gradient Boosting Regressor. The model is trained on historical Reef Check Malaysia survey data (2007-2025) and tested on unseen temporal folds. The residuals represent the difference between the predicted annual change in live coral cover (pp/yr) and the actual observed change across 40 monitoring units.
  [COMPUTATION STEPS]:
    1. Perform time-series cross-validation by iteratively training on data up to year T and predicting for year T+1.
2. Calculate the error (residual) for each monitoring unit prediction: (Actual Change - Predicted Change).
3. Aggregate all residuals across all units and time folds into a single pooled distribution.
4. Identify the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of this distribution to define the 95% confidence interval of [-16.25, +13.66] pp/yr.
  [INTERPRETATION]:
    This range quantifies the model's predictive uncertainty. A residual of 0 indicates a perfect prediction. The asymmetric bounds reflect the model's tendency to occasionally underestimate extreme decline events or overestimate recovery, consistent with the MAE of 5.862 pp/yr.
  [CITATIONS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports, OpenDOSM Data Catalogue

