=== [Judge Iter 0139] 2026-09-16 13:27:39 | Rubric Focus: Validation Rigor ===
Judge Question: "How is the 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution of [-16.25, +13.66 pp/yr] computed?"
Context: Island=Redang, Tab=diagnostics
Model Defense (2.64s) | Title: Model Uncertainty Analysis: Residual Distribution | Pose: answer | Links: 1
  [METHODOLOGY]:
    The 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution is derived from a temporal out-of-sample validation process. The Gradient Boosting Regressor is trained on historical Reef Check Malaysia survey data (2007-2024) and tested against the 2025 hold-out set. Residuals are calculated as the difference between the predicted annual change in live coral cover (pp/yr) and the observed actual change across all 40 monitoring units.
  [CALCULATION STEPS]:
    1. Perform a rolling-window cross-validation where the model predicts the subsequent year's coral cover change.
2. Compute the error (residual) for each of the 404 monitoring-unit rows.
3. Aggregate the residuals into a pooled distribution to capture the ensemble's predictive variance.
4. Identify the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of the error distribution to establish the 95% confidence interval of [-16.25, +13.66 pp/yr].
