=== [Judge Iter 0144] 2026-09-16 13:28:15 | Rubric Focus: Feature Engineering ===
Judge Question: "What is the base prediction value across all units, and how do factor contributions sum to the final output?"
Context: Island=Redang, Tab=overview
Model Defense (3.66s) | Title: Model Methodology: Gradient Boosting Regressor | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [BASE PREDICTION]:
    The model utilizes a global intercept representing the mean annual change across all 40 monitoring units. This baseline is adjusted by the sum of individual feature contributions derived from the Gradient Boosting Regressor.
  [FACTOR CONTRIBUTION CALCULATION]:
    Contributions are calculated using Tree-Path Decomposition (Saabas 2014). The process follows these steps:
1. Trace the decision path of a specific unit through every tree in the ensemble.
2. Attribute the change in predicted value at each split to the specific feature used for that split.
3. Aggregate these path-specific credits across all trees to determine the total contribution of Substrate, Fish, Reported Impacts, Prior Cover, and Geography.
4. Sum the baseline intercept and all feature contributions to arrive at the final predicted annual change (pp/yr).
  [MODEL PERFORMANCE]:
    The ensemble achieves a Mean Absolute Error (MAE) of 5.862 pp/yr, with a 95% pooled forward-test residual distribution ranging from -16.25 to +13.66 pp/yr.
