Judge Question: "Explain how fold-local median imputation works and why global imputation would invalidate results."
Context: Island=Perhentian, Tab=overview
Model Defense (3.97s) | Title: Methodology: Fold-Local Median Imputation | Pose: answer | Links: 0
  [FOLD-LOCAL MEDIAN IMPUTATION]:
    ReefSafe utilizes fold-local median imputation to handle missing monitoring data within the Gradient Boosting Regressor. By calculating the median value specifically from the same monitoring unit or geographic cluster (fold) rather than the entire dataset, the model preserves the localized ecological variance inherent to specific reef sites.
  [RISKS OF GLOBAL IMPUTATION]:
    Global imputation would invalidate results by introducing significant bias through the following mechanisms:
1. Homogenization: It masks site-specific ecological stressors, effectively flattening the variance between healthy and degraded reefs.
2. Statistical Distortion: It artificially pulls outlier data points toward the national mean, leading to underestimation of urgent priority sites.
3. Model Degradation: It introduces noise that obscures the feature importance of local variables, rendering the Tree-Path Decomposition (Saabas 2014) unreliable for identifying specific drivers of coral decline.

