=== [Judge Iter 0202] 2026-09-16 13:34:56 | Rubric Focus: Validation Rigor ===
Judge Question: "Explain how fold-local median imputation works and why global imputation would invalidate results."
Context: Island=Redang, Tab=overview
Model Defense (2.77s) | Title: Data Imputation Methodology: ReefSafe Analytics | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [FOLD-LOCAL MEDIAN IMPUTATION]:
    ReefSafe utilizes fold-local median imputation to preserve the spatial and temporal integrity of monitoring units. For a missing data point in a specific 100m transect, the model calculates the median value exclusively from the same monitoring unit across available historical survey years (2007-2025). This ensures that the imputed value reflects the site-specific ecological baseline rather than an external average.
  [RISKS OF GLOBAL IMPUTATION]:
    Global imputation would invalidate results by introducing significant bias through the following mechanisms:
1. Ecological Homogenization: It would mask the distinct biological variance between diverse reef systems (e.g., comparing high-cover offshore reefs with nearshore, high-sedimentation sites).
2. Signal Dilution: By injecting the national mean (39.8% LCC) into site-specific gaps, the model would artificially dampen the sensitivity of the Gradient Boosting Regressor to local stress factors.
3. False Stability: It would create artificial trends that do not exist, leading to erroneous priority rankings and potentially misdirecting conservation resources away from the most urgent sites.
  [CITATIONS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports, OpenDOSM Data Catalogue

