  [METHODOLOGICAL CONSTRAINTS]:
    1. The model identifies priority for urgent field verification based on historical trends and environmental indicators.
2. Tourism is represented via proxy data (visitor spending and marine park arrivals) rather than direct site-specific impact measurements.
3. The model's MAE of 5.862 pp/yr reflects the inherent complexity of marine ecosystems, where non-linear feedback loops prevent precise attribution of coral loss to any single human activity.
  [DATA SOURCES]:
    Attribution analysis relies on integrated datasets from Reef Check Malaysia annual surveys, DOSM economic indicators, and Department of Environment water quality reports.
  [CITATIONS]: Reef Check Malaysia annual reports, OpenDOSM Data Catalogue

