=== [Judge Iter 0237] 2026-09-16 13:38:33 | Rubric Focus: Economic Methodology ===
Judge Question: "Critique your reef-adjacent economy formula: why is a 10% global coefficient appropriate for Malaysia?"
Context: Island=Kapas, Tab=overview
Model Defense (5.50s) | Title: Critique of Reef-Adjacent Economy Attribution | Pose: answer | Links: 2
  [METHODOLOGICAL BASIS]:
    The 10% coefficient is a conservative proxy derived from Spalding et al. (2017) to isolate reef-attributable expenditure from broader tourism spending. It acknowledges that while marine parks attract visitors, total spending includes non-reef activities (e.g., accommodation, dining, transport). This prevents overestimation of reef-dependent economic value.
  [MALAYSIAN CONTEXT]:
    The RM60.09M annual visitor spending proxy is a localized estimate using the 2024 Domestic Tourism Survey average of RM410 per visitor. It serves as a lower-bound cash flow indicator, distinct from the RM8.7 Billion/year Total Economic Value (TEV) benchmark established by the DMPM (2011-2015), which captures non-market ecosystem services.
  [LIMITATIONS]:
    The 10% coefficient is a static global benchmark. Future iterations of ReefSafe aim to refine this using site-specific survey data to better reflect the unique economic contribution of individual archipelagos like Kapas, where reef health is a primary driver of visitor retention.
  [CITATIONS]: DOSM Domestic Tourism Survey 2024, Marine biodiversity economic valuation

